# Strict Anti-AI-Slop Rules

## 1. Visual & Layout Constraints
- DO NOT use generic dark mode gradients like `#09090b` with glowing neon purple/cyan accents.
- DO NOT use boring, symmetrical hero sections with two side-by-side identical buttons.
- Use asymmetrical layouts (like Bento Grid or 60/40 splits) and ample whitespace (`py-20` to `py-32`).
- Avoid heavy glassmorphism (`backdrop-blur`) and generic rounded cards with thin borders.

## 2. Typography & Colors
- Colors: Use a curated palette (e.g., warm monochrome, high-contrast earth tones, or crisp modern light/dark contrast).
- Typography: Use distinct heading fonts (e.g., Serif or bold sans-serif with proper letter spacing), not standard unstyled default fonts.

## 3. Micro-details & Copy
- No generic AI copy like "Empower your workflow" or "Unlock your potential".
- Ensure clean CSS structure and smooth hover transitions.